Modifications in this derivative work (cell2location-fast), relative to
upstream cell2location version 0.1.5:

1. GPU performance optimizations (by the upstream-fork authors of the
   "cell2location_optimized" snapshot this repository is based on):
   - Added cell2location/models/_cell2location_torch_module.py: a Pyro-free,
     pure-PyTorch re-implementation of the spatial-mapping model's ELBO.
   - torch.compile (reduce-overhead), bfloat16 GPU data preloading, fused
     Adam optimizer, init_to_mean initialization.
   - GPU-backed data splitter and related training-loop changes in
     cell2location/models/base/_pyro_mixin.py.
   - TF32 / cuDNN-benchmark enablement and minor NumPy compatibility fixes.

2. Initialization bug fix (2026, Alistair Turcan):
   - _cell2location_torch_module.py: variational scale parameters are now
     initialized to the unconstrained value softplus^-1(init_scale) =
     log(expm1(init_scale)) instead of the raw value init_scale, so that
     after the softplus transform the effective initial posterior scale is
     exactly init_scale (0.1), matching Pyro AutoNormal's
     PyroParam(0.1, constraint=softplus_positive). Previously the effective
     initial scale was softplus(0.1) ~= 0.744 (7.4x too large) on all 17
     latent sites. See validation/torch_module_init_fix.patch.

